<title>USA: Chrysler to offer flexible-fuel minivans - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Chrysler to offer flexible-fuel minivans - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chrysler Corp plans to begin equipping more than a third of its future minivans to run on ethanol or gasoline, the Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>In Tuesday's electronic edition, the Journal said the plan is scheduled to begin in the 1998 model year, which begins this fall.</p>
<p>That would put Chrysler in the same company as rival Ford Motor Co, which also has plans to commercialize so-called &quot;flexible-fuel&quot; vehicles.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
